[Music]  we're here with Tim CTO from tech  Ellucian will be sharing with us a bit  more about tech Ellucian and how they  implement anthos but first Tim can you  tell us a bit more about what tech  Ellucian does and what it means to be a  Google cloud partner sure well first of  all thanks mark for having me on the  show it's great to be here  Tech Ellucian helps companies come in  modernize their application stack and  really come up with a strategy on how to  get to the cloud and then we'll go in  set up their cloud environment for them  make sure it's secure and ready to be  you know start deploying applications to  and then we'll even run manage services  at the end if they're interested I work  with a lot of companies and they really  really want to modernize a place and  they want to run containers and they  want to run in their data center or  maybe multiple cloud providers and with  the options that out there are really  limited and they all have some sort of  drawback and some sort of you know  things that really stop you from working  with it whereas that though it really  doesn't I mean there's a lot of amazing  things with it it's based on open source  technology it's you know frees you from  the vendor lock and you can deploy it to  many clouds it has the power of gke so  it helps you run the cloud for you and  it really is it's not that expensive so  there's just a lot of benefits to it  that makes sense for how anthos can help  people but how does it actually do those  individual things anthos is actually a  collection of tools oh I should say a  collection of mostly open-source tools  which even brings a lot of more power to  it so first you have gke on prem which  brings you the power of gke and you know  all those benefits like I said that  Google brings forward for you you know  manages the clusters for you it allows  you that scalability and all the amazing  things going to come along with it  second you got the emphasis of  configuration management which is a  great piece of technology that allows  you to treat your configurations as code  so you can check them into the  repository and make changes and when you  want to change or update the system and  automatically pull it down the next is  the anthos service mesh which is a  product based on sto which allows you to  kind of get some insight into your inter  process communication between your  containers and get some insight into  actually what's going on next on the  list you have a cloud run which is a  server list technology that allows you  to bring the functions and the you know  the serverless benefits you get to your  data center to a other cloud provider  and then finally you have the  marketplace so if you need to use you  know third-party tools like MongoDB  Retta sore elasticsearch or any of the  things that are actually in the  marketplace or you can bring those to  wherever you're actually one man goes so  it makes sense these different pieces  kind of play together to create a really  great solution for a wide variety of use  cases can you talk a bit more about how  you've implemented anthos in a specific  use case and like what that brought to  the table absolutely anthos is still  relatively - new technology you know it  just came out last April so you know  people are still learning to you know  get their hands around and figure out  how it works so we've been working with  a lot of customers and when they get  embark on this journey by themselves you  know and they don't properly plan and  strategize how they're gonna do this  they kind of run into problems and we've  saved many customers coming in and  helping them strategize so we're able to  come in set up a plan use some of our  automation in our IP that we've created  and helped them get to anthos in 30 days  or less  another good scenario that we worked  with which is very very specific one as  we were working with a client and the IT  operations guy probably had a little too  much power than he should have and he  was you know working with the  environment and he was in a qualen  vironment at least he thought he was in  a quality environment but he was  actually in a production environment and  he accidentally deleted the namespace  and you can't imagine what the  repercussions of that were  so with anthos if he was running anthos  and and that was configuration manager  he wouldn't have had that problem  because if you delete the namespace it  will automatically go back to the single  source of truth aka the repository pull  the latest version of whatever it was  and rebuild a cluster for you so  actually after we deployed anthos for  him we actually showed him this and had  him actually do it and he was amazed at  how quick it actually rebuilt the  cluster right in front I'm sure that's a  situation that unfortunately a lot of us  can relate to fortunately yes but it  kind of gives a good example of where  the power of anthos and implementing it  comes from so for people who are  interested in in maybe taking on anthos  or learning more about it what are some  of the big takeaways for them sure the  biggest thing that I think that you kind  of don't necessarily think about is it  really brings the cloud to you allows  you to modernize in place so if you want  to run containers and micro services and  you want to run that in your data center  or really any cloud provider that you  choose it brings that keep abilities for  you and it brings all the power of gke  and the management of that it's also  great for companies that are have  problems with a there are regulations  whether there be  data regulations or government  regulations where they got to keep all  the data in one place you know you can  bring the cloud to them where you don't  have to get the data out you know some  of the big takeaways that I've you know  learnt from actually setting up and  installing anthos is you know make sure  that you have full logging enabled I  mean you need to be able to see every  log item that goes in whether it's info  or debug you know the more logging you  have the better you'll be and second you  know when you're actually going in and  setting this up you need to be really  good at recreating this you need to be  able to wipe it clean start fresh and  just keep going in and plugging away  it's always great to hear these customer  stories so thank you so much for coming  in and telling us a bit more about what  makes Antho so powerful thanks buck  thanks for having me if you'd like to  learn more about tech Ellucian visit  Tech illusion comm thanks for watching  and stay tuned for more great episodes  of stack chat

